CVA6ConfigDcacheByteSize = 32768 Signal Flow Tree (32KB 8-way Configuration)
===========================================================================

1. CONFIGURATION PHASE (cv32a6_imac_sv32_config_pkg.sv)
   └── localparam CVA6ConfigDcacheByteSize = 32768;
       └── cva6_cfg.'{ DcacheByteSize: unsigned'(CVA6ConfigDcacheByteSize) }

2. BUILD/DERIVATION PHASE (build_config_pkg.sv)
   └── CVA6Cfg.DcacheByteSize = 32768
       ├── DCACHE_INDEX_WIDTH calculation:
       │   └── $clog2(CVA6Cfg.DcacheByteSize / CVA6Cfg.DcacheSetAssoc)
       │       └── $clog2(32768 / 8) = $clog2(4096) = 12
       │       └── Standard calculation (not forced to 0)
       │
       └── DCACHE_NUM_WORDS calculation:
           └── 2 ** (DCACHE_INDEX_WIDTH - DCACHE_OFFSET_WIDTH)
               └── 2 ** (12 - 4) = 2 ** 8 = 256 words per way

3. MODULE INSTANTIATION PHASE
   └── std_cache_subsystem (core/cache_subsystem/std_cache_subsystem.sv)
       └── wt_dcache (core/cache_subsystem/wt_dcache.sv)
           └── wt_dcache_mem (core/cache_subsystem/wt_dcache_mem.sv)
               └── parameter DCACHE_CL_IDX_WIDTH = CONFIG.DCACHE_INDEX_WIDTH = 12

4. SIGNAL WIDTH IMPACT
   └── DCACHE_CL_IDX_WIDTH = 12
       ├── rd_idx_i [DCACHE_CL_IDX_WIDTH-1:0] → [11:0] (12-bit signal)
       ├── wr_cl_idx_i [DCACHE_CL_IDX_WIDTH-1:0] → [11:0] (12-bit signal)
       └── cl_index [DCACHE_CL_IDX_WIDTH-1:0] → [11:0] (12-bit signal)

5. MEMORY ORGANIZATION IMPACT
   └── SRAM Instantiation (wt_dcache_mem.sv)
       └── for (genvar i = 0; i < DCACHE_SET_ASSOC; i++)
           └── sram #(.NUM_WORDS(DCACHE_NUM_WORDS))
               └── NUM_WORDS = 256 (256 entries per way)
               └── 8 SRAM instances (one per way)
               └── Each SRAM has depth = 256

6. CACHE GEOMETRY
   └── 32KB Cache Organization:
       ├── Total Size: 32768 bytes
       ├── Line Size: 128 bits = 16 bytes
       ├── Total Lines: 32768 / 16 = 2048 lines
       ├── Ways: 8
       ├── Sets: 2048 / 8 = 256 sets
       └── Address mapping: 256 sets × 8 ways × 16 bytes

7. ADDRESS DECODING
   └── Address field extraction (32-bit address):
       ├── Offset: addr[3:0] (4 bits) → byte within line
       ├── Index: addr[11:4] (8 bits) → selects one of 256 sets  
       └── Tag: addr[31:12] (20 bits) → identifies cache line

8. PERFORMANCE IMPACT
   └── 32KB Cache Benefits:
       ├── Higher hit rate than smaller caches
       ├── 256 sets reduces conflict misses
       ├── Working set fits in cache for many applications
       ├── Reasonable SRAM area for embedded systems
       └── Good balance of size vs access time

KEY RELATIONSHIPS:
- DcacheByteSize = 32768 creates 32KB total cache capacity
- With 8 ways: 32768 / 8 = 4096 bytes per way
- INDEX_WIDTH = 12 bits addresses 4096 locations
- NUM_WORDS = 256 per way (4096 bytes / 16 bytes per line)
- Provides 16x more capacity than 2KB configuration